cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the underlying mathematics and, if
  applicable, this implementation. The optimal strategy, exact distribution,
  mean, variance, central limit theorem, large-deviation principle and phase
  transitions implemented here are due to Clay, Kuba and Tripathi
  (arXiv:2607.10418). This repository is an independent reference
  implementation / research playground and is not authored by the paper's
  authors.
title: "ShuffleLab: a reference implementation and experimentation framework for the single-shelf shuffle and optimal card guessing"
abstract: >-
  ShuffleLab implements the asymmetric single-shelf shuffle and the optimal
  complete-feedback card-guessing strategy of Clay, Kuba and Tripathi, together
  with Monte-Carlo experiments, exact distributions, and an interactive demo.
authors:
  - name: "ShuffleLab contributors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/example/shelfshuffle"
url: "https://github.com/example/shelfshuffle"
keywords:
  - card shuffling
  - shelf shuffle
  - card guessing
  - complete feedback
  - optimal strategy
